WEBVTT

00:37:58.756 --> 00:38:01.516
There was a real possibility
of nuclear confrontation

00:38:01.556 --> 00:38:03.476
between the world's two superpowers.

00:38:03.796 --> 00:38:06.796
At least for the last 30 years,
there’s been no chance of that.

00:38:06.836 --> 00:38:08.836
Functionally, no chance of that.

00:38:08.876 --> 00:38:10.476
I think we're now back in a world

00:38:10.476 --> 00:38:13.316
where a Cuban Missile Crisis
is again a reality.

00:38:13.356 --> 00:38:17.236
Now, that doesn't mean that I think
nuclear war is likely or imminent.

00:38:17.276 --> 00:38:18.436
I don't.

00:38:18.436 --> 00:38:19.756
And in fact,

00:38:19.796 --> 00:38:23.596
there is active deconfliction
going on even today:

00:38:23.636 --> 00:38:26.236
the Americans and Russians
with a new hotline,

00:38:26.276 --> 00:38:28.596
the secretary general of the UN,

00:38:28.636 --> 00:38:31.476
with the Russian defense minister